# .gitattributes — per-path git behaviour overrides.
#
# Memofun ships only small plaintext files; no LFS, no special merge
# drivers, no release artifacts that need a custom diff. The only
# thing worth setting is the line-ending default for collaborators
# who develop on Windows: without this, every `git diff` from a
# Windows machine shows the entire file as changed because LF gets
# converted to CRLF on checkout and back to LF on commit. The repo
# convention is LF everywhere; this attribute just keeps that
# invariant even on Windows contributors.
#
# Same shape as the sibling apptonomia / sinonimia / calculia / etc.
# repos' .gitattributes (which all use `* text=auto eol=lf` for the
# same reason).
#
# Add per-path overrides below if the project ever needs something
# more specific (LFS, a binary with no diff, etc.).

# Default for everything: store as LF, normalise line endings on
# checkout, don't try to do anything clever with non-text files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Sweep explicit overrides for known-binary file extensions.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
*.gz binary
*.br binary